Dear Ms. Ilves, dear Yusra,

Please allow me to introduce myself. My name is Hana Kobayashi-Reyes, and
I joined Kestrow as Privacy Officer last week. Among the files I have
inherited is the review of the Tinderbox course assistant pilot, and Yusra
has kindly told me that you are the architect for it, Ms. Ilves. I am
writing to both of you so that the campus lead has the same information.

Some context on our process, since it may be new to the system office.
Any new service at Kestrow that processes personal information about
students or staff goes through the campus privacy impact assessment (PIA)
before that processing begins. The PIA is a structured questionnaire
covering what data is collected, the purpose and legal basis, where the
data is stored and for how long, who can access it, which third parties
or shared services receive it, and how individuals are informed. My
office reviews the completed questionnaire, may come back with questions
or conditions, and records the outcome in the campus register. It is
separate from, and in addition to, the security review led by the system
office.

1. PIA questionnaire. I would be grateful if you could complete the
   attached PIA questionnaire for Tinderbox by Friday 12 March. As the
   architect you are best placed to answer most of it; where a question
   concerns campus practice (for example, the notice given to students in
   the pilot courses), please mark it and I will follow up with Yusra.

2. PIA walkthrough. Could you also set up a 30-minute
   data-flow walkthrough with me before you fill it in? Think of it as
   a PIA walkthrough: you would show me how data moves between the learning
   management system, the course assistant and the shared platform it is
   hosted on, and I can tell you early which parts of the questionnaire
   will need the most detail. Any time that suits you over the coming
   days is fine; my calendar is still fairly open.

For the avoidance of doubt: under campus policy, real student data cannot
be processed in Tinderbox until both the PIA and the security review are
complete. I understand from Yusra that the pilot is currently running on
dummy data, which is entirely consistent with that.

I look forward to working with you both, and I apologise for arriving in
the middle of things.

With kind regards,

